3. Deep Audit: Flaws, Bugs, Fake Data & Limitations
A. The "Fake Data / Simulated Data" Audit
Component	What it Contains	Is It Fake?	Defense & Evaluation
Fare Quotes (Live)	Live quotes scraped from IndiGo & Air India	REAL (100%)	Verified against live search availability. Carries data_origin = 'observed' and SHA-256 body hash.
Synthetic Gap-Filler	Fills un-scraped cells	CALIBRATED ESTIMATE	Calibrated to DGCA historical route averages. Crucially, it is explicitly tagged data_origin = 'imputed' and excluded from the index calculation view (observed_fare_quotes).
Route Weights	Passenger traffic per route	OFFICIAL DGCA DATA	Loaded from data/dgca/city_pair_pax_fy24.csv with SHA-256 hash. No fabricated constants.
DGCA Backtest Data	2023–2026 Monthly Fares	OFFICIAL DGCA DATA	Extracted from DGCA Monthly Traffic & Fare Monitor reports.
B. Current Limitations & Edge Cases
Forward-Only Scraped History: Web scraping is inherently forward-looking; no scraper can retroactively scrape fares from 2022. Our system handles this honestly by using DGCA historical reports for the backtest and real scrapers for forward validation.
Dynamic Web Markup Dependency: Airline booking engines periodically update HTML structure. While our selector engine uses resilient text-pattern matching (₹[0-9,]+ with carrier validation), structural changes require periodic connector health checks.
Headless Anti-Bot Boundaries: Direct airline search funnels use aggressive Cloudflare/Akamai bot blockers. Our connectors solve this by querying public travel search listing pages without stealth browser spoofing or proxy evasion (maintaining strict SIH ethics compliance).
